<h2 id="pins">Pin assignments</h2>
<p class="lede">These must match <code>Core/Config/PinMap.cs</code> and <code>docs/gpio-map.md</code>.</p>

<div class="build-note danger">
    <div class="build-eyebrow">Three ways to lose a day</div>
    <p>
        <strong>ADC2 is dead while WiFi is on.</strong> The soil probe must be on ADC1 (GPIO 32–36, 39).
        This is the most common ESP32 sensor bug and it presents as a sensor that worked on the bench.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>nanoFramework's 1-Wire runs over a UART, not a bit-banged pin.</strong> It needs a COM
        port's RX <em>and</em> TX tied together to the DQ line, with a 4.7 kΩ pull-up to 3V3. Without
        the pull-up the bus reads all-ones and every probe enumerates as absent.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>Record the DS18B20 ROM IDs explicitly.</strong> Do not rely on enumeration order.
        Getting it wrong is silent: the controller heats to the outworld probe and cooks the nest, or
        heats to the nest-top probe and never reaches setpoint. Neither looks like a wiring fault.
    </p>
</div>

