<h3>Why the float switch reads LOW for full</h3>
<p>
    The switch is wired to ground and read against the internal pull-up, so a risen float reads LOW.
    That direction is chosen, not convenient. A broken wire floats HIGH, which reads <em>not full</em>,
    which asks for a refill — and that refill is bounded twice over, by the runtime limiter and by the
    fact that the reservoir cannot physically hold a harmful dose. The opposite polarity would read
    <em>full</em> forever on a broken wire, silently stop hydrating the colony, and look perfectly
    healthy on this dashboard. Fail-safe here means failing toward a bounded action, because doing
    nothing is what kills a colony slowly.
</p>

